===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|kangooroo|kanguroo|kanguru||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|kky|gangurru||eastern grey kangaroo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|kăng-gə-ro͞oʹ}}, {{IPA|en|/kæŋ.ɡə.ˈɹuː/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-kangaroo.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q5070208}} A member of the {{taxfmt|Macropodidae|family}} family of large [[marsupial]]s with strong [[hind leg]]s for [[hopping]], native to [[Australia]]. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=w:James Cook|journal=Journal|date=4 August 1770|titleurl=http://www.gutenberg.org/etext/8106
|passage=Besides the Animals which I have before mentioned, called by the Natives '''Kangooroo''', or '''Kanguru''' […].}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1814|author=w:Matthew Flinders|title=A Voyage to Terra Australis
|passage=In the woods are the '''kanguroo''', the emu or cassowary, paroquets, and a variety of small birds […].}}
# {{lb|en|Canada|attributive}} A [[hood]]ed [[jacket]] with a front [[pocket]], usually of [[fleece]] material, a [[kangaroo jacket]].

